# Pixel Canary (Callstack Apex) — findings by Iceman

- Source: Callstack / Apex (`callstack/apex`, formerly stealth "Pixel Canary")
- Date: 2026-11-14 (UTC), deep second-pass research
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** Pixel Canary / Apex
- **Short description:** Apex is Callstack’s closed agentic coding model specialized for mobile/web React workloads (React Native, React, Next.js), revealed from the stealth name “Pixel Canary” per local metadata; it has verifiable vendor/gateway specs and framework-specific eval claims but lacks standardized, comparable public benchmarks across this project’s core scoring dimensions.
- **Provider / access:** Callstack (API access) and Vercel AI Gateway (`callstack/apex`). Local metadata lists `callstack/apex`, `noFreeId`; prior “free while stealth” claim is treated as unverified in metadata.
- **Release / knowledge:** Vercel AI Gateway page lists release date 2026-10-08. Knowledge cutoff not explicitly stated in reviewed sources.
- **IDs:** `pixel_canary`, `Pixel Canary`, `Apex`, `callstack/apex`.
- **Context window:** 262,144 tokens context window; 131,072 max output (Vercel AI Gateway/model listing). Apex site describes a 256K context window in page copy (minor source wording conflict).
- **Modalities:** Text and image input; text output (Vercel AI Gateway/model listing indicates image input support).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-14):** $0.50 per 1M input tokens, $0.20 per 1M cached input tokens, $3.00 per 1M output tokens (Apex site/Vercel AI Gateway listing; excluding applicable taxes/provider terms).
- **Architecture:** Proprietary closed model. Architecture and parameter count not publicly disclosed.

### Raw benchmarks found

> SECOND-PASS SELF-EXCLUSION (updated): I reviewed `apex.callstack.com`, Vercel AI Gateway’s Apex model page, models.dev API/search, OpenRouter/Artificial Analysis/Hugging Face searches, and the metadata-referenced Callstack blog URL (404). I found attributable vendor/gateway specs and vendor-reported React/Next.js framework eval results for the exact Apex/`callstack/apex` model, but no independently verifiable standardized benchmark coverage suitable for comparable project scoring (e.g. SWE-bench Verified/Pro, LiveCodeBench, SciCode, Terminal-Bench 2.1, τ²/τ³, GPQA Diamond, HLE, AIME, AA Intelligence Index/AA-LCR, multimodal suites). Because evidence is strong for a specialized domain but insufficient for standardized cross-dimension 1–100 comparability, this file remains `.md.excluded` (notes only; scores ignored).

Framework-specific / vendor-reported coding evals (Apex site, attributed to RN/Next.js eval sources shown on page):

- **React Native evals:** **87.8%** (Apex), compared on-page to Claude Opus 5.5 88.6% and GPT 6.1 Sol 86.3% (source cited on page: `rn-evals.vercel.app`).
- **Next.js evals (31 tasks, pass@4, per page):** **96.8%** with docs, **90.3%** without docs (Apex). Page also reports cost/leaderboard comparisons (e.g. Apex $0.067* per task vs GPT 6 Astra $0.891 and Claude Opus 5.5 $0.234; source cited as `nextjs.org/evals`, Sep 25, 2026, per page footnote).
- **React fix benchmark context (ReactBench, as shown on page):** Apex shown as tied #2 in “fixing React” section (exact task/effort breakdown partially extracted from page content; treat as vendor-reported UI claim pending direct benchmark-page verification).

Agent / tool use:

- Tool/agentic coding capability implied by product positioning and API use; no standardized Terminal-Bench/τ-bench/GDPval-AA/MCP-Atlas scores found.

Reasoning / knowledge:

- GPQA Diamond / HLE / MMLU-Pro / AIME / AA Intelligence Index / AA-LCR / CritPt: **no verified public score found**

Coding (standardized):

- SWE-bench Verified / SWE-bench Pro / LiveCodeBench / SciCode: **no verified public score found**

Long context:

- 262K context / 131K max output listed by Vercel AI Gateway; no standalone long-context retrieval benchmark score found.

Multimodal:

- Image input supported (text/image in, text out per Vercel AI Gateway); no multimodal benchmark scores found.

### Normalized scores (1–100)

Not provided. Verifiable evidence exists for specialized React/Next.js coding performance and model specs/pricing, but not for standardized, comparable benchmark coverage across the repo’s core dimensions. No scored assessment is issued and this report remains self-excluded.

### Source comparison / conflicts

- **Identity:** `apex.callstack.com`, Vercel AI Gateway, and models.dev API align on Callstack Apex (`callstack/apex`) as a React Native/React/Next.js-focused coding model; local metadata maps this folder to stealth “Pixel Canary”.
- **Specs:** Vercel AI Gateway lists 262K context / 131K max output, text+image input, $0.50/$0.20 cached/$3.00 output pricing; Apex site states “256K context window” in copy (minor wording/context discrepancy).
- **Benchmarks:** Apex site reports strong vendor-attributed React Native and Next.js eval results (87.8% RN; 96.8%/90.3% Next.js), but metadata-referenced Callstack blog URL returned 404 and no standardized public benchmark suite results were found in AA/OpenRouter/HF/models.dev scans in this pass.
- **Catalogs:** models.dev API contains `callstack/apex`; OpenRouter/AA/HF searches in this pass did not provide rich standardized benchmark entries for this exact model.

